# Uniform by-reference capture (F3 / B2 parity guard). A closure `f` that captures a by-reference
# local (`x`, a cell) is invoked inside a `spawn` task via the call form `spawn f()`. Whichever way
# the task's copy of `f` and its cell are reconstructed, BOTH engines must agree — the print is
# post-join, so serial == M:N == `7` exactly.
#
# NOTE (deliberate, do not "fix"): the design's mutation-form F3 (`f := fn(): x = x + 1`) is NOT
# expressible in Chezzi — closures are EXPRESSION-only, so a closure value can never reassign a
# captured scalar cell. Because a closure cannot mutate its captured cell, the "shared vs isolated
# cell" distinction across the airlock is unobservable, so no serial-vs-M:N divergence can arise from
# a cell-bearing closure. (A captured closure VALUE is otherwise rejected as non-sendable by the
# checker; only `spawn f()` / `Executor.submit` cross a callable, and those stay consistent.)
fn main():
    x := 7
    ch := Channel[int]()
    f := fn(): ch.send(x)
    parallel:
        spawn f()
    print(ch.recv())            # 7 — serial == M:N

main()
